WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.225
Runs and state.

2
00:00:01.225 --> 00:00:05.236
The router compares each notice with
its state, which is keyed by the

3
00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:09.175
provider and the provider's I D and
holds each notice's fingerprint.

4
00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.438
A task-routed notice gets a
create the first time it's open.

5
00:00:12.438 --> 00:00:14.310
It gets an update when it changes,

6
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.638
meaning a different fingerprint,
or when its rule changes.

7
00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:19.749
An unchanged notice writes nothing.

8
00:00:19.749 --> 00:00:24.224
When the provider closes its notice,
the task gets a close payload,

9
00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:28.863
but that close asks for the re-read,
clause C4; it doesn't close the task.

10
00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:31.700
The task is resolved on
the agency's own check.

11
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.168
And an open notice from a provider read
in this run that's no longer listed

12
00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:40.487
is marked absent, and its task gets an
update asking for the same re-read.

13
00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:44.887
A provider that wasn't read this run
never has its notices marked absent.

14
00:00:44.887 --> 00:00:47.678
Each run writes the payloads, a task list,

15
00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:51.313
a routing spreadsheet file,
the state and a manifest.

16
00:00:51.313 --> 00:00:55.970
It's a dry run: nothing is sent unless
the scheduled run's send switch is given,

17
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.440
with sending turned on in the settings.
